## Rules (strict for repeatable output)
- Produce a PRESCRIPTIVE sequence: each entry is one concrete automatable action plus its verification.
- Split compound Zephyr steps into separate sequence entries; merge redundant ones.
- "action" = imperative device-level instruction (configure X, send Y, power-cycle, read output of 'show ...').
- "verify" = the concrete observable check that proves the action worked (exact CLI output fields, packet fields, link state). This becomes self.passed()/self.failed() logic.
- "zephyr_step_idx" = the 1-based index of the source Zephyr step above (the step it was derived from).
- Skip steps that cannot be automated on a testbox (physical cable wiggling, visual LED checks) but list them in "notes" so the reviewer sees what was dropped.
- Output JSON ONLY, no prose, in this exact shape:
{"sequence": [{"n": 1, "action": "...", "verify": "...", "zephyr_step_idx": 1}], "notes": "anything skipped or assumed"}
